/// known-gap: interp has no aspects; the interpreter is being retired
/// Two aspects may name the same field. The same starting value in both
/// is no clash, and neither is the same bare `~` trait. A field one aspect
/// leaves bare takes the value the other gives, whether the aspects come
/// before or after the class.
aspect Rich |
    gold: 1
    ~pride
    army
xx
<>Town |
    uses Rich, Proud
xx
aspect Proud |
    gold: 1
    ~pride
    army: 10
xx
t <> Town | name: "a"
:say("{t >> gold} {t >> pride} {t >> army}")
